# Toyota Prius XW30 five-door hatchback, 2009-2016.
#
# The third-generation Prius. UK sales launch August 2009 at £18,370 for the T3,
# on the road; sold through 2016, when the XW50 replaced it.
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Prius-gen3-UK-launch-pack-2009.pdf
# https://media.toyota.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/pdf/Prius-archive-timeline.pdf
#
# Dimensions 4.460 x 1.745 x 1.480 m, wheelbase 2.700 m. Source: English
# Wikipedia, "Toyota Prius (XW30)" infobox, 2010-2011 figures; the late-2011
# facelift grew the car by about 20 mm in length and 10 mm in height, and the
# pre-facelift car is the one modelled. The hull measures 4.460 x 1.745 m with
# the roof at 1.480 m and the wheel centres 2.700 m apart (60.5 per cent of
# length). Mirrors and plates extend beyond the hull.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's image 1 is a shallow front-left three-quarter,
# not a true elevation, so the flank was built from it and from images 2 to 4
# with the wheel centres fixed by the published ratio. A true elevation was
# rendered for the Gate B comparison.
#
# Colours are Toyota GB brochure names, evidence grade (a): the July 2009
# brochure lists Pure White, Tyrol Silver, Astral Black, Novus Grey, Orion
# Blue, White Pearl and Vermillion Red; the March 2012 brochure adds Cabernet
# Red and Dark Blue. Four common British finishes are modelled: Tyrol Silver,
# Pure White, Astral Black and Orion Blue. The 2009 launch pack calls the grey
# "Abyss Grey"; the brochure's Novus Grey is the British name, and that
# discrepancy is recorded here though the grey is not modelled. Weights silver
# 3, white 3, black 2, blue 2, total 10, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the car's quoted maximum. Comfort 110/345, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 110: roomier and quieter than the XW20, a step below the XW50.
# Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: August 2009 intro, retires staggered 2021-2024 on a
# twelve- to fifteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw30.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/toyota-prius-xw30.dae (73 objects). References:
# citycars/references/toyota-prius-xw30/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the front bumper corners are squarer than the
# photographs and the headlamp faces read thin; the tail lamp clusters are
# narrower and the rear bumper flatter than the real car's; the side-window
# divisions are more angular. The top view confirms a continuous
# body-coloured roof between the windscreen and the upper hatch glass. At
# 128 px the wedge nose, the rising belt line and the split rear glazing read
# as the third-generation Prius.

obj=citycar
name=ToyotaPriusXW30(TyrolSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2009
intro_month=8
retire_year=2024
retire_month=6
